<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <!--
    Fleet.Api (C058 fleet-svc-org + C059 fleet-svc-fleet-ops) — the whole Fleet Portal surface:
    the Verification-Officer-gated organisation, its Owner/Manager/Viewer sub-roles, the bank &
    payout profile every rupee of Mode B money depends on, and the operations on top of it —
    Mode A/B vehicle onboarding with AL-50's named document slots, time-bounded driver assignment,
    tracker binding, scheduling with the US-13.11 not-started alarm, the live map, analytics,
    geofences and the Epic 23 subscription proxies.

    FENCE 1: a fleet operates Mode A and/or Mode B. **Never Mode C** (AL-03). Held in the
    database — `registry.fleet_vehicles.mode CHECK (mode IN ('A','B'))` (migration 0306) — and
    re-stated in `FleetModes`, so no code path here can put a fleet on the on-demand plane.
    FENCE 2: **an unapproved org onboards nothing.** Held structurally: every vehicle and
    assignment route hangs off the two groups `FleetEndpoints` builds with
    `.RequireApprovedFleet()`, so C059's routes are gated the moment they are mapped rather than
    each remembering. `Every_vehicle_and_assignment_route_is_gated` asserts it by walking the
    endpoint data source.
    FENCE 3: **a cross-org read is a security bug.** Held in Postgres — migration 1806's
    RESTRICTIVE policies over the five org-owned tables, entered through `SET LOCAL ROLE
    mageride_fleet_reader`. The application's own `WHERE fleet_id = @FleetId` is the second lock,
    not the only one.

    FENCE 4 (C059): a required AL-50 document slot holds a vehicle out of APPROVED — registration,
    insurance and revenue licence for every mode, plus the route permit for Mode A. Held in
    VehicleApprovalService, which re-derives every slot inside the transaction that writes the
    status, so a permit that lapsed while the queue item sat there stops the approval.

    Not this component's: monthly invoicing and the fleet wallet are C060's; the Verification
    Officer's *screen* is the Admin Portal's (C107) behind admin-bff (C062), which drives the
    internal plane here. Route-deviation and geofence *alerting* is Phase 3 — the CRUD is built and
    nothing raises an alert.

    No Redis, no Kafka, no outbox — see FleetApplication for why each is off.

    Verify: dotnet test backend/src/Fleet.Api.Tests -c Release
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>MageRide.Fleet</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>MageRide.Fleet.Api</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <UserSecretsId>mageride-fleet-api</UserSecretsId>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\MageRide.Shared\MageRide.Shared.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Dapper" />
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Fleet.Api.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
